{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9dc-8c63-7ec2-bcbf-e7bc396a275e"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"37e460c4-f4d7-4321-aad6-659e2238ed1f","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"37e460c4-f4d7-4321-aad6-659e2238ed1f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"37e460c4-f4d7-4321-aad6-659e2238ed1f"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260916-235lb7, status=development)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `developer` (`implementer`) — Writes code, fixes bugs, writes tests\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `swiftui`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/swiftui/SKILL.md`\n- `core-data`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/core-data/SKILL.md`\n- `go-testing-tools`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Compose only independently accepted mapper/test bytes onto freshly fetched PR6 head; verify exact prospective tree and preserve prior signed ancestry and fixture diagnostics.\n- [ ] Create explicit signed commit by Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com> using /Users/iv/.ssh/ivanopcode with current timestamps; verify locally and on GitHub after feature-branch publication.\n- [ ] Observe actual hosted CI for the published exact head and attach complete outcome with evidence, distinguishing success, new product failure and external execution failure honestly; no main landing or false-green claim.\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260916-235lb7\n- **Title:** TASK-260916-235lb7: publish-reviewed-wifiaware-delta-and-observe-pr6-ci\n- **Parent:** STORY-260715-anxje6\n\n### Description\n\nAfter independent acceptance of BUG-260916-20xt79 rev2, compose its reviewed mapper/test delta onto fresh PR6 head, preserve all prior signed commits and fixture diagnostics, create and verify Ivan Oparin signed commit, publish feature head and observe real hosted CI. Report exact outcome honestly, including any new failure. This phase does not land or claim complete delivery; TASK-260908-34gi0y retains full exact-head review, green-checks and landing obligations.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nPublished head tree matches independently reviewed prospective composition, with prior signed ancestry preserved and local/GitHub signatures verified; actual hosted CI outcome and evidence captured; no default-branch landing, fake status, new code repair or VPN operation.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260916-235lb7_publish-brief.md\n> Publish accepted exact prospective tree and observe genuine CI\n\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/TASK-260916-235lb7/TASK-260916-235lb7_publish-brief.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2865`\n- Content digest: `sha256:c1f847a8019b417274b016cce80fddaa1f76ec498137c28716d5a253f2543e27`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260916-235lb7_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260916-235lb7, name=TASK-260916-235lb7_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260916-235lb7 --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n"}}
